  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Scholarships for students from his native Ilia were an early expression of John Latsis's public giving. The Greek shipping entrepreneur established a dedicated scholarship foundation in 1967, helping young people pursue higher education. He also created the Fondation Latsis Internationale, which recognised scientific achievement through prizes for researchers and research teams.\n\nEmergency relief gave his philanthropy a practical dimension. After the Kalamata earthquake, he provided temporary accommodation for displaced residents and donated a factory for prefabricated housing. He financed a purpose-built primary school for Athens College and initiated a specialist burns centre at Elefsina. The burns unit was completed after his death and became part of the public hospital system.",
    "html": "<p>Scholarships for students from his native Ilia were an early expression of John Latsis's public giving. The Greek shipping entrepreneur established a dedicated scholarship foundation in 1967, helping young people pursue higher education. He also created the Fondation Latsis Internationale, which recognised scientific achievement through prizes for researchers and research teams.</p>\r\n<p>Emergency relief gave his philanthropy a practical dimension. After the Kalamata earthquake, he provided temporary accommodation for displaced residents and donated a factory for prefabricated housing. He financed a purpose-built primary school for Athens College and initiated a specialist burns centre at Elefsina. The burns unit was completed after his death and became part of the public hospital system.</p>\r\n",
